  {
    "id": "anno-mineyama_lower_p075_left-12",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "此米六石六斗二合五勺"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "この米　六石六斗二合五勺"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "'This [gold] in rice': 6.6025 koku — the rice equivalent of the combined gold total, printed full-size in the same column. NOTE: transcribed as printed, but almost certainly a 1928 compositor's 斗-for-升 substitution. The table's own rate is exactly 8 ryō/koku (永 7,053.12 mon → 此金 7.05312 ryō → 此米 0.88164 koku on lower_p076_right; 7.05312/0.88164 = 8.00000), which converts the 48.5 ryō here to precisely 6.0625 koku = 六石六升二合五勺 — the same glyph string with 升 for 斗. With 6.0625 the domain's 合米 chain closes to within 0.00018; with the printed 6.6025 it is off by 0.54."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "正雜合金此米"
      }
    ],
